  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I was looking through the world review queue for public worlds today and noticed a VRChat homekit world got declined as sited in this screenshot https://gyazo.com/8c781663df37244417ffaf302580edce .  I even checked the official homekit download page to see that there was no mention of this not being allowed to be made public. https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrchat-home-kit\n. This creates an unfair position for world creators that would have read into to use case scenario for the world kit. Getting declined isn't really what i'm getting at here really, its more so me asking if VRChat could provide what we are \"allowed\" to do and what we are \"not\". People put a lot of time and effort into worlds and this could upset a few people if they were unaware from the start.",
